   "title": "READ ME FIRST",
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## Repeat loop demo \u2014 runs out of the box (no models, no API keys)\n\nPress **Run**. The loop body executes **3 times** (iterations widget on\nRepeat Open); each pass appends one \"x\" to the carried string, so the\nfinal preview shows **xxxx** (the start \"x\" + 3 passes).\n\nHow it works:\n- **Repeat Open -> Repeat Close** re-execute everything between them.\n- \"value\" slots carry data from one pass to the next.\n- Only 2 loop wires are required: flow_control + your value slots.\n  The count lives in the *iterations widget* (it must stay a widget,\n  not a connection).\n- Watch the terminal: the pack logs every pass\n  (\"[Repeat Open] pass 2 of 3 ...\").\n\nBelow: **Lazy Switch** \u2014 flip the toggle and only the chosen branch\n*ever executes* (the other is bypassed, not just ignored)."
   ],
   "widgets_values_named": {
    "text": "## Repeat loop demo \u2014 runs out of the box (no models, no API keys)\n\nPress **Run**. The loop body executes **3 times** (iterations widget on\nRepeat Open); each pass appends one \"x\" to the carried string, so the\nfinal preview shows **xxxx** (the start \"x\" + 3 passes).\n\nHow it works:\n- **Repeat Open -> Repeat Close** re-execute everything between them.\n- \"value\" slots carry data from one pass to the next.\n- Only 2 loop wires are required: flow_control + your value slots.\n  The count lives in the *iterations widget* (it must stay a widget,\n  not a connection).\n- Watch the terminal: the pack logs every pass\n  (\"[Repeat Open] pass 2 of 3 ...\").\n\nBelow: **Lazy Switch** \u2014 flip the toggle and only the chosen branch\n*ever executes* (the other is bypassed, not just ignored)."
   },
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
